# Go Code

- Prefer deletion, reuse, and consolidation before new code.
- Reuse existing packages (`internal/memory`, `internal/pack`, `internal/store/postgres`).
- Use structured APIs/parsers over fragile string manipulation.
- Avoid cleverness; optimize for readable diffs.
- Avoid new dependencies unless they clearly remove more complexity than they add.
- ASCII quotes only in code and comments.

## Vertical packs (Brainy)
- Domain labels live in `packs/{vertical}/v1/pack.yaml`, not as Postgres `kind` enums.
- Runtime fields: `primitive`, `vertical`, `label`, `metadata`, `lifecycle_state`.
- Marketing/finance terms (`brand_rule`, `thesis`) are pack vocabulary, not new Go types or DB enums.
- See `docs/vertical/verticalization-model.md` before extending the memory model.
